gets bigger rather than smaller as he eats it.

1215
01:03:20.130 --> 01:03:22.230
Because they use different takes.

1216
01:03:22.630 --> 01:03:28.590
So at 12 minutes, 21 seconds, all that's left is like a little corner of bread.

1217
01:03:28.750 --> 01:03:32.250
And then at 12 minutes, 28 seconds, it's much larger.

1218
01:03:32.510 --> 01:03:33.330
I love it.

1219
01:03:33.470 --> 01:03:36.770
I love how into this episode our kids were with background catches.

1220
01:03:37.150 --> 01:03:37.730
I know.

1221
01:03:38.350 --> 01:03:39.230
It's so cute.

1222
01:03:39.850 --> 01:03:43.190
Well, lady, I want to talk about the scene with Michael and Angela.

1223
01:03:43.930 --> 01:03:45.650
They're in the break room.

1224
01:03:46.170 --> 01:03:49.070
And they're clearly both missing Dwight.

1225
01:03:49.230 --> 01:03:53.030
But obviously, neither of them are saying that to each other.

1226
01:03:53.310 --> 01:03:56.910
And Michael just says, oh, it's good to have Oscar back.

1227
01:03:57.230 --> 01:03:58.370
And Angela's like, yeah.

1228
01:03:58.630 --> 01:04:02.830
And they both just sort of sadly take a sip of their beverage and look off into space.

1229
01:04:02.830 --> 01:04:09.530
And I never, ever got quiet moment scenes with Steve.

1230
01:04:09.970 --> 01:04:15.890
And so in rewatching this, it was so special to me because I just, our characters hardly

1231
01:04:15.890 --> 01:04:16.890
ever interacted.

1232
01:04:16.890 --> 01:04:19.650
And when they did, I was usually mad at him, you know?

1233
01:04:20.110 --> 01:04:20.390
Yeah.

1234
01:04:20.570 --> 01:04:21.790
So that was really special.

1235
01:04:21.790 --> 01:04:32.710
And then on a total tangent, there is a fantastic shot at 13 minutes, 47 seconds of Luanne's water fountain.

1236
01:04:32.710 --> 01:04:35.050
And it's there, like, gurgling away.

1237
01:04:36.210 --> 01:04:38.810
Lady, I saw the same thing.

1238
01:04:39.010 --> 01:04:40.610
I saw the same thing.

1239
01:04:41.110 --> 01:04:45.850
I think that's what was in the background of that kitchen scene in that other episode that we all

1240
01:04:45.850 --> 01:04:46.890
thought was a fireplace.

1241
01:04:47.310 --> 01:04:49.590
I think it was Luanne's water feature.

1242
01:04:49.870 --> 01:04:52.810
She had a Zen garden and a water fountain.

1243
01:04:53.090 --> 01:04:53.610
She did.

1244
01:04:53.750 --> 01:04:55.710
And they never plugged it in because it made noise.

1245
01:04:55.870 --> 01:04:59.090
But every once in a while, I guess, it got plugged in.

1246
01:04:59.230 --> 01:05:03.910
And I think you're right because it has a little blue light in it.

1247
01:05:03.950 --> 01:05:04.170
Yes.

1248
01:05:04.350 --> 01:05:06.850
That maybe we thought was a fire something.

1249
01:05:07.290 --> 01:05:07.750
Yes.

1250
01:05:08.450 --> 01:05:09.110
Oh, my God.

1251
01:05:09.110 --> 01:05:11.590
I love that we both got excited about Luanne's fountain.

1252
01:05:12.130 --> 01:05:18.390
Well, Jenna, I think on that note of getting super excited about a fountain in the background,

1253
01:05:18.970 --> 01:05:20.230
we should take a break.

1254
01:05:21.110 --> 01:05:22.030
Yeah, we'll take a break.

1255
01:05:22.150 --> 01:05:24.490
And then we'll come back and get into this big prank.

1256
01:05:29.170 --> 01:05:31.030
All right, guys, we are back.

1257
01:05:31.470 --> 01:05:32.750
Angela, do you know what I'm doing right now?

1258
01:05:33.810 --> 01:05:34.210
No.

1259
01:05:34.470 --> 01:05:36.470
I mean, I can see you, but...

1260
01:05:36.470 --> 01:05:37.630
I'm making bread.

1261
01:05:37.870 --> 01:05:41.010
I can't see your hands, but I know your left one is moving.

1262
01:05:41.010 --> 01:05:44.850
No, I'm not literally making bread in my lap.

1263
01:05:46.470 --> 01:05:52.810
I'm sitting here podcasting, but I am simultaneously bread making.

1264
01:05:53.110 --> 01:05:58.530
Like, that's the cool thing about bread making is that I have dough that is rising into a little

1265
01:05:58.530 --> 01:06:03.610
living dough baby that I'm going to put in my oven and turn into crisp, delicious sourdough

1266
01:06:03.610 --> 01:06:03.850
bread.

1267
01:06:03.850 --> 01:06:08.430
As we speak, that science is working in my kitchen on my counter right now.

1268
01:06:08.630 --> 01:06:11.210
During this break, I molded my little dough baby.

1269
01:06:12.110 --> 01:06:12.570
Aw.

1270
01:06:12.990 --> 01:06:13.290
Yeah.

1271
01:06:13.450 --> 01:06:15.850
Well, I molded another dough baby.

1272
01:06:16.130 --> 01:06:17.610
I like to call my belly.

1273
01:06:18.230 --> 01:06:22.070
Um, because I went downstairs and ate a little piece of this.

1274
01:06:22.210 --> 01:06:24.370
I don't even know what it is that Josh made.

1275
01:06:24.470 --> 01:06:25.610
It's like some kind of...

1276
01:06:25.610 --> 01:06:28.050
It tastes like a little square of pecan pie.

1277
01:06:28.270 --> 01:06:28.970
It's so good.

1278
01:06:29.310 --> 01:06:33.070
Can we give a plug to Josh's baking page, please?

1279
01:06:33.390 --> 01:06:37.790
Baking with Josh and Ange, there is a recipe on there for something called a brookie.

1280
01:06:38.570 --> 01:06:39.170
Mm-hmm.

1281
01:06:39.170 --> 01:06:41.950
Okay, you know, I made this the other day.

1282
01:06:42.170 --> 01:06:48.630
It is a layer of brownie topped with a layer of chocolate chip cookie and their bars.

1283
01:06:49.510 --> 01:06:53.810
Angela, I ate so many of them that I made myself sick.

1284
01:06:53.990 --> 01:07:00.230
I made myself sick like I was like a child who couldn't stop eating candy on Halloween.

1285
01:07:00.530 --> 01:07:02.950
And I felt so ill.

1286
01:07:02.950 --> 01:07:09.210
And even when I felt sick from eating so many of them, I wanted to eat more of them.

1287
01:07:09.370 --> 01:07:10.990
That's how good the brookie is, guys.

1288
01:07:11.150 --> 01:07:14.430
It'll make you sick and you won't care and you'll keep eating it anyway.

1289
01:07:14.690 --> 01:07:19.210
I don't know what kind of endorsement that is, but I feel like that's a good endorsement.

1290
01:07:20.370 --> 01:07:22.530
Yeah, well, he has tons of recipes.

1291
01:07:22.610 --> 01:07:23.830
You guys, my husband is a baker.

1292
01:07:24.110 --> 01:07:27.930
You can go to bakingwithjoshandange.com for all of his recipes.

1293
01:07:28.190 --> 01:07:30.810
I don't even know why I'm in the equation there.

1294
01:07:30.810 --> 01:07:33.430
It's just that when he bakes, he likes me around.

1295
01:07:34.810 --> 01:07:36.310
But he is the master.

1296
01:07:36.610 --> 01:07:38.990
I'm the taste tester and he's the master.

1297
01:07:39.230 --> 01:07:40.670
That was really sweet, Jenna.

1298
01:07:40.810 --> 01:07:45.270
Well, if you want to eat so much of something that you make yourself sick, make the brookie.

1299
01:07:45.570 --> 01:07:48.130
But he also has, guys, not just sweets.

1300
01:07:48.130 --> 01:07:50.970
He's got like these one sheet meals.

1301
01:07:51.550 --> 01:07:55.590
And I love to cook things on one sheet because then I only have to clean one thing.

1302
01:07:56.090 --> 01:07:57.310
Yes, they are really good.

1303
01:07:57.330 --> 01:07:59.450
We just did his one sheet chicken fajitas.

1304
01:07:59.690 --> 01:08:00.290
That's my favorite.

1305
01:08:00.930 --> 01:08:01.890
It's so good.

1306
01:08:02.210 --> 01:08:02.510
All right.

1307
01:08:02.650 --> 01:08:06.950
This became a small commercial for bakingwithjoshandange.com, but I stand by it.

1308
01:08:07.970 --> 01:08:08.790
Well, thanks.

1309
01:08:08.970 --> 01:08:09.930
That's really sweet.

1310
01:08:09.930 --> 01:08:10.550
I'll tell him.

1311
01:08:10.670 --> 01:08:11.250
He'll be tickled.

1312
01:08:11.970 --> 01:08:12.550
All right.

1313
01:08:12.650 --> 01:08:14.370
Well, let's get back to this episode.

1314
01:08:14.890 --> 01:08:18.010
Jim steals Andy's cell phone.

1315
01:08:18.210 --> 01:08:18.390
Yeah.

1316
01:08:18.570 --> 01:08:20.630
But why does he pass it off to Pam?

1317
01:08:20.750 --> 01:08:22.910
I don't understand why they trade it twice.

1318
01:08:23.490 --> 01:08:24.790
What are they, secret spies?

1319
01:08:24.790 --> 01:08:31.010
Couldn't he have just taken it and gone straight to the bathroom and like chucked it up in the ceiling or something?

1320
01:08:31.350 --> 01:08:31.510
Yes.

1321
01:08:31.690 --> 01:08:34.190
This entire prank could have been done by Jim alone.

1322
01:08:34.370 --> 01:08:41.390
He tried to recruit all these people to do this prank with him that required only one person.

1323
01:08:41.590 --> 01:08:43.190
He could have pranked Andy on his own.

1324
01:08:43.190 --> 01:08:48.030
But for Jim, the prank is like the social bonding experience.

1325
01:08:48.030 --> 01:08:51.290
It's not about like just doing it by himself.

1326
01:08:51.690 --> 01:08:52.870
What's the fun in that?

1327
01:08:53.010 --> 01:08:53.290
Exactly.

1328
01:08:53.910 --> 01:08:54.090
He wants a partner.

1329
01:08:54.270 --> 01:08:54.930
He wants a buddy.

1330
01:08:55.110 --> 01:08:55.470
Yes.

1331
01:08:56.330 --> 01:09:04.450
So, he does this weird thing where he knocks over the pens and steals the phone and then gives it to Pam and then Pam gives it back to him.

1332
01:09:05.030 --> 01:09:06.870
And Karen clocks it.

1333
01:09:07.030 --> 01:09:07.170
Yeah.

1334
01:09:07.350 --> 01:09:08.010
Karen notices.

1335
01:09:08.330 --> 01:09:11.370
She doesn't know what they're doing, but they're in cahoots.

1336
01:09:11.590 --> 01:09:11.970
Well.

1337
01:09:12.090 --> 01:09:16.330
And then you're like his lookout, but you can clearly see him.

1338
01:09:16.550 --> 01:09:21.470
You guys have the most, like you're the most oddball like duo.

1339
01:09:21.470 --> 01:09:26.910
I feel like there could have been a spinoff where Jim and Pam are secret spies, but everyone knows.

1340
01:09:27.070 --> 01:09:37.790
Well, and just to our point earlier, is no one noticing the camera crew following Jim and Pam sneaking and like filming them do this prank?

1341
01:09:38.070 --> 01:09:42.510
There's a lot of disbelief you have to suspend right here in this moment.

1342
01:09:42.750 --> 01:09:47.690
Jenna, no one sees it because Pam is so great at distracting them by drinking her water.

1343
01:09:50.900 --> 01:09:52.220
That's all we see.

1344
01:09:52.220 --> 01:09:54.520
Hey, Pam's just drinking her water and playing with her necklace.

1345
01:09:54.880 --> 01:09:55.760
Nothing to see here.

1346
01:09:55.860 --> 01:09:56.060
Yeah.

1347
01:09:56.540 --> 01:09:57.440
What do you mean?

1348
01:09:57.620 --> 01:09:57.840
What?

1349
01:09:58.020 --> 01:10:04.000
Well, you have to remember in the last episode, Phyllis kind of spills the beans and says to Karen,

1350
01:10:04.320 --> 01:10:09.820
I'm so glad you and Jim are together because he was hung up on Pam for so long.

1351
01:10:10.020 --> 01:10:12.840
So, you know, Karen has got that in her brain.

1352
01:10:12.840 --> 01:10:18.300
And when she sees the two of them kind of giggling and up to something, she's like, oh, no, what's happening?

1353
01:10:18.300 --> 01:10:18.900
Yes.

1354
01:10:19.320 --> 01:10:22.500
Well, meanwhile, Kelly and Oscar are setting up for the party.

1355
01:10:22.660 --> 01:10:25.440
I think it's very funny that Oscar has to set up his own party.

1356
01:10:25.560 --> 01:10:27.200
He has chores at his own party.

1357
01:10:28.100 --> 01:10:28.820
It's amazing.

1358
01:10:29.320 --> 01:10:32.180
And then Michael, meanwhile, is pouting in the kitchen.

1359
01:10:32.500 --> 01:10:34.680
He wants to let Jim know that he's not fine.

1360
01:10:35.340 --> 01:10:36.300
He's not fine.

1361
01:10:36.540 --> 01:10:38.280
And he's like, he doesn't want to talk about it.

1362
01:10:38.400 --> 01:10:39.120
But Jim's like, OK.

1363
01:10:39.260 --> 01:10:40.540
And he's like, OK, I'll talk about it.

1364
01:10:40.620 --> 01:10:41.240
He's like, OK.

1365
01:10:41.460 --> 01:10:41.680
Yeah.

1366
01:10:48.300 --> 01:10:49.820
Well, I mean, he's kind of a yes man.

1367
01:10:50.140 --> 01:10:51.780
And Michael's like, that's not true.

1368
01:10:51.780 --> 01:10:55.020
Because when I say I don't like something, he says he doesn't like it, too.

1369
01:10:56.140 --> 01:10:57.300
It's like, oh, Michael.

1370
01:10:58.000 --> 01:10:58.460
Oh, Michael.

1371
01:10:58.960 --> 01:11:01.020
Steve is so brilliant in this episode.

1372
01:11:01.280 --> 01:11:05.580
I know we talk about how good he is so like every week.

1373
01:11:05.580 --> 01:11:16.540
But he had to, I don't even know how to say it, but the way he reacts to Andy is like

1374
01:11:16.540 --> 01:11:19.600
a whole new version of Michael Scott we haven't seen.

1375
01:11:19.860 --> 01:11:21.500
And he's so brilliant.

1376
01:11:22.040 --> 01:11:26.980
And the way he doesn't get things and then the audience gets it before him and then he

1377
01:11:26.980 --> 01:11:27.900
finally gets it.

1378
01:11:28.040 --> 01:11:29.200
It's just amazing.

1379
01:11:29.200 --> 01:11:37.120
Well, Angela, he has this talking head that I can't even barely watch because...

1380
01:11:37.120 --> 01:11:38.260
Is it about the raspberry?

1381
01:11:38.460 --> 01:11:38.760
Yeah.

1382
01:11:38.960 --> 01:11:39.860
The sherbert thing?

1383
01:11:40.120 --> 01:11:43.580
It's about the way Steve delivers it is so masterful.

1384
01:11:43.680 --> 01:11:46.760
But the whole thing just makes me so uncomfortable.

1385
01:11:47.880 --> 01:11:51.340
Whenever Michael talks about his childhood, I get scared.

1386
01:11:51.340 --> 01:12:00.780
I just feel like I don't want more details about his loneliness and his like need for attention

1387
01:12:00.780 --> 01:12:03.240
and his all of it.

1388
01:12:03.500 --> 01:12:06.760
His awkward interactions with his mom and stepdad, Jeff.

1389
01:12:06.960 --> 01:12:07.600
I mean...

1390
01:12:07.600 --> 01:12:07.800
Yeah.

1391
01:12:08.420 --> 01:12:08.920
Yeah.

1392
01:12:09.400 --> 01:12:10.200
I know.

1393
01:12:10.460 --> 01:12:11.280
Poor Michael.

1394
01:12:11.320 --> 01:12:16.020
I know this is totally off topic, but I was impressed that Jim's choice of snack was

1395
01:12:16.020 --> 01:12:16.720
raw carrots.

1396
01:12:17.680 --> 01:12:18.320
Yes!

1397
01:12:18.640 --> 01:12:19.260
Angela!

1398
01:12:19.880 --> 01:12:24.420
Angela, we had a fan point this out about the carrots.

1399
01:12:25.000 --> 01:12:29.300
Brianna Kernan wrote in to say, does John really like to snack on carrots?

1400
01:12:29.300 --> 01:12:34.460
Because he can be seen in multiple episodes snacking on carrots at various times.

1401
01:12:34.840 --> 01:12:36.780
I did a lot of scenes with John.

1402
01:12:36.980 --> 01:12:39.720
And so I can tell you that he eats carrots.

1403
01:12:39.900 --> 01:12:45.580
If given the choice for what he gets to eat in a scene, he will pick something healthy.

1404
01:12:45.780 --> 01:12:48.200
He will pick carrots a lot.

1405
01:12:48.200 --> 01:12:49.040
He would pick carrots.

1406
01:12:49.260 --> 01:12:54.500
To the point that they finally had to say, John, you can't with the carrots.

1407
01:12:54.500 --> 01:12:56.200
It's like really bad for sound.

1408
01:12:56.380 --> 01:12:58.380
So then he started eating grapes.

1409
01:12:59.500 --> 01:13:00.400
Oh, wow.

1410
01:13:00.400 --> 01:13:01.840
So you'll see him eat some grapes.

1411
01:13:01.840 --> 01:13:05.200
But occasionally it would be scripted that we're eating chips.

1412
01:13:05.900 --> 01:13:06.560
Mm-hmm.

1413
01:13:06.760 --> 01:13:08.080
And he would eat the chips.

1414
01:13:08.080 --> 01:13:10.700
But he preferred a healthy snack, guys.

1415
01:13:11.020 --> 01:13:11.720
He just did.

1416
01:13:12.760 --> 01:13:14.620
I am very impressed, John.

1417
01:13:14.900 --> 01:13:15.720
I'm very impressed.

1418
01:13:16.880 --> 01:13:19.960
I mean, I usually would ask for potato chips.

1419
01:13:20.840 --> 01:13:21.200
Yeah.

1420
01:13:21.620 --> 01:13:25.440
Well, BJ Novak and I used to say that if it's a prop, it doesn't have any calories.

1421
01:13:25.440 --> 01:13:27.380
So you can eat as much of it as you want.

1422
01:13:27.900 --> 01:13:29.280
Oh, interesting theory.

1423
01:13:29.420 --> 01:13:29.560
Yeah.

1424
01:13:29.640 --> 01:13:30.460
It's not real food.

1425
01:13:30.600 --> 01:13:31.100
You're pretending.

1426
01:13:31.800 --> 01:13:32.620
It's pretend food.

1427
01:13:32.760 --> 01:13:33.000
It's pretend food.

1428
01:13:33.000 --> 01:13:33.480
No calories.

1429
01:13:34.280 --> 01:13:36.660
You know what I would pick now is a brookie.

1430
01:13:37.260 --> 01:13:39.660
I'd be like, can I snack on a brookie, please?

1431
01:13:40.340 --> 01:13:41.720
Well, the party's set up as underway.

1432
01:13:42.120 --> 01:13:46.020
But Angela and Pam have a little conversation out by the elevators.

1433
01:13:47.080 --> 01:13:51.620
And I loved it so much, Jenna, when Pam's like, is it about Dwight?

1434
01:13:51.820 --> 01:13:54.080
And Angela's like, no, John Denver.

1435
01:13:54.860 --> 01:13:57.420
You're like, OK, that's how it's going to be.

1436
01:13:57.600 --> 01:13:57.980
I'm out.

1437
01:13:58.100 --> 01:13:58.260
Yeah.

1438
01:13:58.420 --> 01:13:59.100
No, no, no, no, no.

1439
01:14:00.480 --> 01:14:03.200
But is John Denver like one of her favorite singers?

1440
01:14:03.200 --> 01:14:04.920
Like, where did John Denver come from?

1441
01:14:05.100 --> 01:14:09.340
It's just such a funny sort of little bit of detail to me about Angela Martin.

1442
01:14:09.780 --> 01:14:13.620
Well, Angela tells Pam that she's really missing Dwight and she feels bad.

1443
01:14:13.960 --> 01:14:16.820
And Pam says, I think you should talk to Michael.

1444
01:14:18.260 --> 01:14:25.300
And Angela's like, Pam, I'm not like you walking around in your provocative outfits saying whatever thought pops in your head.

1445
01:14:25.840 --> 01:14:26.340
Yeah.

1446
01:14:27.360 --> 01:14:27.920
I love that.

1447
01:14:27.920 --> 01:14:35.040
As she's wearing a sweater over a button down, like, what are these outfits, Angela?

1448
01:14:35.220 --> 01:14:36.560
What are you even talking about?

1449
01:14:36.780 --> 01:14:37.100
Yes.

1450
01:14:37.300 --> 01:14:43.420
But anyway, Angela appreciates Pam, you know, talking with her and gives her such a weird hug.

1451
01:14:43.580 --> 01:14:44.940
It's like she hugs her.

1452
01:14:45.060 --> 01:14:47.860
And then when she realizes she's hugging you, she shoves you away.

1453
01:14:48.140 --> 01:14:50.080
Well, we had a fan question about it, Angela.

1454
01:14:50.080 --> 01:14:57.020
Caleb Fiener and Kylie Campbell both ask, was that hug improvised or was it in the script?

1455
01:14:58.740 --> 01:14:59.940
What do you think, Angela?

1456
01:15:00.540 --> 01:15:00.920
Well.

1457
01:15:01.200 --> 01:15:02.220
Improvised or in the script?

